      "message": "A couple of issues here found with the help of Gemini:\n\n1. `pda_pa` was pinned only if `modified.pst \u003d\u003d 1`, not if `irte-\u003epst \u003d\u003d 1` but `modified.pst !\u003d 1`\n2. In this case we fail to actually modify the IRTE, yet we still return success to the host. So we might return e.g. -EAGAIN or whatever?\n\n...Actually, this try_cmpxchg128 failure shouldn\u0027t really happen (since we hold iommu-\u003elock and since IRTEs are only modified by SW, not by HW). So we could just replace WARN_ON with BUG_ON here (thus avoid the need to think how to correctly handle the case when it happens)?",
